# Part 5: Exam Prep Mechanics — **P1**

The section readers land on from Google. Keep it factual and current.

- **Logistics.** Verified on the official page in September 2026 — **re-verify at writing time**,
  these change:

  | | NCP-AIO | NCP-AII | NCP-AIN |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Format | **30 MCQ + 3 hands-on labs** | ~70-75 MCQ | 70-75 MCQ |
  | Duration | 120 min | 120 min | 120 min |
  | Price | $500 | $400 | $400 |
  | Delivery | Online, remotely proctored (Certiverse) | same | same |
  | Result | Pass/Fail | Pass/Fail | Pass/Fail |
  | Valid | 2 years | 2 years | 2 years |

  **AIO is the only hands-on one.** That is the single most useful fact in this article for someone
  choosing between the three, so put it in the intro too, not only here.

- **Lab-exam strategy** — a section that does not exist anywhere else, so write it:
  - Rough budget: ~40 minutes for 30 MCQ, ~80 minutes for 3 labs. Do not burn the lab time on MCQ.
  - The labs are a live CLI on real Slurm / Kubernetes / BCM. Speed on the CLI is a scored skill —
    practise the *typing*, not just the concepts.
  - Know the read-only diagnostic commands cold: `sinfo -R`, `nvidia-smi -q -d ECC`, `dcgmi dmon`,
    `kubectl describe node`, `ibstat`. Orientation is where lab time leaks.
  - Say the honest thing: 3 labs out of a Pass/Fail result means the labs are where the exam is won.

- **Official prep guide + the DLI courses it names** — that is the authoritative scope. Link it and
  tell readers to diff it against this article rather than trusting the article.
- **The honest resource warning.** Unlike NCA-AIIO there is no good free video course and no
  trustworthy practice bank. The source material *is* the docs: BCM Admin Manual, DGX User Guide,
  DCGM docs, NCCL docs, UFM docs, Xid guide. Say that plainly — it is the most useful sentence in the
  section.
- **What is learnable from docs alone and what is not.** Be blunt:

  | Learnable from docs | Needs hardware |
  |---|---|
  | Xid taxonomy, decisions | Recognizing a real failure cascade |
  | DCGM fields and CLI | `dcgmi diag -r 3` output on a bad GPU |
  | GPU Operator architecture | Multi-node NCCL, gang scheduling pain |
  | BCM concepts | `cmsh` muscle memory, provisioning a node |
  | IB commands and theory | Reading `ibdiagnet` on a real fabric |

  And the line that matters: the MCQ half is winnable from the docs column. **The lab half is not.**

- **8-week plan**, mapped to this article:

  | Week | Focus | Sections |
  |---|---|---|
  | 1 | Re-read article 53, fix gaps | 53 Phases 1-8 |
  | 2 | Observability tooling, hands-on | 2.1, 2.2 |
  | 3 | Slurm GPU specifics + Pyxis | 1.3 |
  | 4 | GPU Operator, break and fix it | 1.4, 3.6 |
  | 5 | BCM + DGX OS docs, heaviest reading week | 1.1, 1.2 |
  | 6 | Fabric: IB, NCCL, bandwidth debugging | 2.3, 2.4, 3.1, 3.7 |
  | 7 | Failure modes + optimization | 3.3, 3.4, 3.9-3.11, Part 4 |
  | 8 | Part 6 cheat sheet, blueprint diff, book it | Part 6 |

- **Recertification window**, and the note that Professional certs expire — plan the renewal, do not
  be surprised by it.

