# Appendix B: Capture list — **P1, DO THIS FIRST**

Not a reader section. A note to self, promoted to a real appendix only if it reads well.

These are impossible to reproduce once the cluster access ends, and without them this article becomes
article 53 with different words. Collect opportunistically, store raw, redact hostnames later.

| Capture | Feeds | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `nvidia-smi topo -m` on a real 8-GPU node | 1.3, 3.7 | The single most reusable artifact |
| `ibstat` healthy **and** degraded | 2.3, 3.7 | The degraded one is the rare one — grab it the moment you see it |
| `ibdiagnet` summary | 2.3 | Redact GUIDs |
| `dcgmi diag -r 3` full pass | 2.2 | And a failing one if you ever get it |
| `NCCL_DEBUG=INFO` init log — IB path | 2.4 | Show the transport line |
| `NCCL_DEBUG=INFO` init log — TCP fallback | 2.4, 3.1 | Force it with `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1` |
| `all_reduce_perf` busbw at 1/2/4/8 nodes | 2.4 | The scaling curve. Highest-value single artifact. |
| A real Xid in `dmesg` + `nvidia-smi -q` after | 3.3, 3.4 | Opportunistic — cannot be scheduled |
| `nvidia-smi -q -d ECC` with nonzero counters | 3.4 | Including remapping state if you are lucky |
| `nvsm show health` healthy + unhealthy | 1.2 | |
| `cmsh` session: image → category → overlay | 1.1 | Screen recording is fine |
| `nsys` timeline of a real training step | 4.1 | Export, do not just screenshot |
| Grafana: util 100% vs SM active low | 2.1, 3.2 | **The money shot of the article** |
| Sawtooth util under storage starvation | 3.9 | |
| `nvidia-smi -q -d PERFORMANCE` while throttling | 3.10 | Easiest during a hot afternoon |

**Rule while capturing:** save the raw text, not a screenshot, wherever the output is text. Screenshots
cannot be grepped, redacted or reflowed for mobile.

